  "source_unit_note": "FR-322 \"Clause source unit\", FR-778-AC-8..FR-778-AC-11 (TC-1890): a timestamped-event clause row keyed by declaration c, whose source_unit names the source unit that declares the clause. The reader resolves the row's timestamp_unit in that unit only; subject.declared_by is the unit that declares the clause's subject and is never read. time_units lists, per declaring unit identity, the units of dimension Time it declares (each linear: s, and ms = 1/1000 s). Every case's clause holds one duration count aggregate whose bounds are typed by the unit named in bound_unit.",
